  "findings": {
    "consumer": "402 native Rust tests passed, one ignored; 77 JavaScript tests passed; 93 rendered browser checks and 163 captures passed, including trusted cancel/drag, Back/reopen, explicit acceptance/save, signed swivel, all five System checks, DPR2/DPR1 and offline.",
    "platforms": "All three full desktop builds passed and saved cold caches. ARM Android passed attempt1; mounted Android passed the sole unchanged-source rerun after the separately retained radio-state failure. iOS passed both bundles, all native/portable checks, seven same-process observations and six warm activations.",
    "framework": "Standalone framework Linux failed the new bounded-year resize centering regression and the existing carousel backward-wrap test. Generic coherent-metric reentry, bounded keyboard/gesture, and both native cancel/reopen regressions passed. Other framework native/browser jobs passed.",
    "baseline": "The separate framework conventions failure is the independently reproduced stale C++ headers on unchanged merge base21720a379. It does not explain or excuse the two runtime regressions.",
    "followup": "Rebind the native realized picker window when resize changes its first value or pool. Preserve child-owned transient wrap/overscroll offsets when the effective presenter offset is unchanged. Existing failing assertions remain intact; one focused generic ownership regression is added."
